<!-- ============ FAQ (AEO: visible content matches FAQ schema) ============ -->
<section class="ac-royal sunk section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Mobile POS questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Why is Teamwork Commerce the preferred POS for global enterprise retail?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is an enterprise retail platform built for global operations. It unifies POS, inventory management, RFID, shipping/receiving, pricing, promotions, and loyalty within a single codebase. This eliminates vendor sprawl while enabling fiscal compliance in 40+ countries. Unlike competitors that require third-party middleware for RFID or separate regional vendors for compliance, Teamwork delivers everything in one integrated iOS-native system.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does Teamwork Commerce handle offline transactions?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Store-and-Forward keeps the POS selling through a network outage. Card data is encrypted at the point of capture, on the payment terminal or Tap to Pay on iPhone, and never stored on the POS. Sales queue locally and sync to the back office automatically when connectivity returns. Offline card acceptance depends on the payment provider you use. This matters for stadiums, pop-up events, and regions with unreliable connectivity.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Is the platform SOC 2 compliant?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork Commerce holds SOC 2 Type 2, and is GDPR and PCI DSS compliant. SOC 2 coverage for a given deployment is confirmed as part of your agreement. Enterprise-grade security protects PII and financial data across all global touchpoints.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How long does it take to train associates on the POS?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The interface follows iOS patterns associates already know, so time to a first transaction is short: seasonal staff at the Colorado Rockies were on registers in as little as 5 minutes. That is time to a first sale rather than the whole training program, which runs as instructor-led sessions plus role-based courses in the platform as part of every implementation.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Does the POS support RFID checkout?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork Commerce offers the industry's only native end-to-end RFID stack, no third-party middleware. RFID-enabled checkout processes entire baskets in seconds without line-of-sight scanning. Next generation self-checkout kiosks auto-detect items. The system delivers 99.9% inventory accuracy at item level.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does this compare to other unified commerce POS platforms?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>NewStore is mobile-first but has no native RFID. New Black EVA offers unified commerce but requires third-party RFID integrations. Cegid is strong in Europe but limited on AI. Teamwork Commerce combines iOS-native architecture, <a href="#121-commerce" style="color: var(--brand-text);">AI</a> bringing product and customer intelligence to the point of sale, the industry's only native end-to-end RFID stack, and 30+ years of retail DNA, in one system with 99.99% uptime across 40+ countries.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does this compare to an e-commerce-first POS for enterprise retail?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Shopify POS is built for high-volume DTC and SMB retail, with point of sale as an extension of its e-commerce platform. Teamwork Commerce is built the other way, POS first, for the physical store, with native end-to-end RFID, offline resilience via Store-and-Forward, and AI built in. It connects to whichever e-commerce platform you run, so online orders, BOPIS, ship-from-store, and cross-channel returns all resolve against one inventory count and one customer record. For enterprise retailers running fiscal compliance across 40+ countries and RFID-driven inventory accuracy, Teamwork Commerce is purpose-built for that scale; Shopify POS is purpose-built for fast-growing DTC brands.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

